<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  The launcher icon: Anodex's own mark on the near-black field it uses everywhere.

  The art is not redrawn here. It is the desktop app's `src/renderer/assets/title-logo.png` — the
  same "A" AnodexLogo shows on the app's chrome — trimmed and scaled so its whole bounding box fits
  inside the circle every launcher mask keeps, and exported per density. Regenerate rather than edit by hand if
  the brand mark ever changes.

  The monochrome layer is a flat silhouette taken from the mark's alpha, because themed icons are
  tinted from the user's wallpaper and a violet-to-blue gradient survives that badly. Keeping the
  alpha keeps the cut-out counter of the A, which is what makes it recognisable at a glance.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_field" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
